    "An agent is judged by CI: the workflows that run the tests, the lint and type settings, the test runner's configuration, the coverage limits, and the verify scripts an agent runs before it says it is done. If an agent can edit any of those, it can pass by making the judge easier instead of making the code right. You saw this in the lesson on checks an agent cannot weaken. The first wall is already in place: the agents' GitHub App has no workflows permission, so GitHub itself refuses a push that touches .github/workflows. The locked-checks check covers everything else.",
