   "Friday, 18:40. The orchestrator, the Temporal worker that claims VMs and drives every run, crashes in the middle of a CI-fixer run and comes back with a bug that keeps it from resuming that run. Its sandbox VM, a full-size machine, keeps running. Nothing is wrong with the VM itself; it is simply that nobody is using it anymore, and nobody remembers it is there. At about 42 cents an hour it would cost twenty dollars by Monday, and it is still a machine with our code on its disk.",
