    "text": "# fcp\\n\\nRhino Health's Federated Computing Platform in one repo: the cloud API, the on-prem client that runs\\ninside customer networks, the Python SDK and the dashboard.\\n\\n## Where things live\\n- \`cloud/rhinoCloud/\`: cloud API (Django, DRF, Celery). Main app \`rhinoCore/\`.\\n- \`client/rhinoOnPrem/\`: on-prem client (Django, gRPC, RQ). It reaches the cloud over a reverse gRPC stream.\\n- \`common/fcp_common/\`: shared code, including the gRPC protos in \`rhinoAgentRpc/\`.\\n- \`sdk/\`: the public \`rhino_health\` package. Read \`sdk/CLAUDE.md\` first.\\n- \`frontend/\`: the dashboard (Next.js, React). Read \`frontend/AGENTS.md\` first.\\nArea rules in \`.claude/rules/\` load by themselves when you open files in that area.\\n\\n## Run and check\\n- \`poe --help\` lists the dev tasks. Backend unit tests: \`scripts/local_run_backend_unit_tests.sh cloud\`.\\n- Frontend: \`npm run lint\`, \`npm run check-types\`, \`npm run test:unit\` in \`frontend/\`.\\n- Use fake seed data only, never real customer data.\\n\\n## Changes and PRs\\n- One change per PR. Title: \`[FE] RH-1234: what changes for the user\` (\`[BE]\` for backend).\\n- Cloud, client and sdk CI run on push; frontend CI runs on pull requests.\\n\\n## Knowledge\\nHow does X work, or why is it like this? Use the \`kb\` skill. It searches the R&D brain\\n(RhinoHealth/rnd-kb) and cites pages as path@sha. If a page is wrong, propose a fix.",
