   "Three required checks run on every fcp PR from the ai-agents-checks image, pinned by digest, called from a thin workflow in fcp pinned by commit SHA: independent-approval (one approval from someone outside the requester set, on the head commit), locked-checks (fails an agent PR that changes a path in settings/protected-paths.yaml or the QA checks listed in the PR body's locked-checks block), and weakened-tests (annotations only, on every PR). The same protected-paths file feeds the PreToolUse hook in the VM, and the rhino-ai-agents App has no workflows permission and no bypass on the fcp ruleset.",
   "For routines, the harness runs the false-heal check before the scope judge, adds the charter's never-rules (for example no added retries or sleeps for the flaky-test fixer), and also runs it from the Stop hook so the agent sees the problem before it calls itself done. Any finding ends a routine run as false_heal and moves the routine back a stage."
