   "h": "Who runs what",
   "p": [
    "Three things are involved: the Temporal Service, a worker and a client. The Temporal Service is a server with a database. It stores what happened in every run, and it holds task queues, which are named lists of work waiting to be done. It never runs your code. A worker is your own Node process: it connects to the service, keeps asking one task queue for work, and runs your workflow and activity code when work arrives. A client is any code that starts a run or sends one a message; for us that is the Jira poll and the Slack app.",
    "Now the flow. The Jira poll, as a client, asks the service to start ticketToPr with the ID nova:RH-1234. The service records the start and puts a task on the queue ai-agents-nova. A worker that listens on that queue takes the task and runs the function until the first await, where the workflow asks for writePlan. That request goes onto the queue as well, a worker runs writePlan, and its result is recorded. Then the workflow reaches the sleep, and the worker has nothing to do for this run until the timer fires."
   ],
